{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>The nesher.</b> This too is a bird known by this name in the language of Ishmael. There is evidence that this is so because the two languages are close." "<b>The peres.</b> Even though there is a lone opinion that it is not found in settled lands, the Gaon [Saadia] erred in translating it al-'anqa, for this name in the language of Ishmael refers to a thing not found in the world, that never was and was never created, but exists only as a parable. And so the scholars of their language will concede. If so, it is impossible that He would prohibit by name a thing that never was."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Reading ראיה as 'evidence'; the phrasing יש כדמות ראיה ('there is something like evidence') is rendered as 'there is evidence.'"}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:24.507261791Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}